! conclusion: Re-enter after exit only when the prior loss was repaired and the next probe is bounded.

  + context: **Play grain.** P1 previously stopped offering after a snatch, and
    the institution has since produced an observable remedy.

  + IF:
    The seized tokens were restored or compensated, the remedy is recorded, and
    a small new offer can test whether play changed.

  + HOWEVER:
    Permanent exit discards any improvement the institution achieved, while
    re-entry on a promise alone repeats the original exposure.

  + THEN:
    Re-enter with the smallest discriminating give-and-ask pair and expand only
    after an accepted exchange.

  + BECAUSE:
    Observed repair supplies evidence that the loss path has changed; the bounded
    probe tests whether the counterpart's response changed without assuming it.
